# Security and privacy

- Authenticate every data API. Enforce RBAC and ethical walls server-side.
- Never return raw secrets in APIs, diffs, audits, logs, exports, or browser
  state after submit. Store `secret_reference` identifiers only.
- `/admin` is admin-only. Non-admins must receive 403 from the API even if
  they guess the URL.
- Do not silently weaken security, privacy, audit completeness, legal hold,
  or verified-cell preservation settings.
- Redact Authorization headers and secret-shaped values in audit metadata.
- Client documents must never be sent on AI “Test Connection” calls.
